# proto-file: protowire/schema/v1/report.proto
# proto-message: protowire.schema.v1.Report
#
# Golden validation report (RFC-001 §6.4, §7) for the collections
# fixture: per-element validation on repeated and map fields, including
# the map KEY dimension (issues #141/#153).
#
#   schema:   15_collections_golden/inventory.proto
#   instance: 15_collections_golden/instance.textproto
#
# engine and wall_time_nanos are excluded from cross-port equality and
# omitted here. Violation order (§6.4): fields in declaration order;
# within one map entry, the key dimension precedes the value dimension —
# the §8 lowering carries key rules on the synthetic entry's `key = 1`
# field and value rules on `value = 2`, so per-entry evaluation follows
# the entry's field order. Element-type rules precede the field-level
# collection rule (base → derived → field-level).
#
# Pins per violation:
#   1. Key violation: same subscripted path as the value violation of
#      the SAME entry — for_key = true is what disambiguates them (§7);
#      actual_value is the key the rule evaluated. (This violation is
#      spec-authored and leads the reference engine: protocheck does
#      not yet validate the key dimension — trendvidia/protocheck#53 —
#      and its wire conversion predates for_key —
#      trendvidia/protocompile#116.)
#   2. Value violation: for_key unset; actual_value is the entry value.
#   3. Repeated element: `index` subscript, alias chain provenance.
#   4. Collection-level rule: unsubscripted path, no actual_value (the
#      collection itself is not captured as a Value), RULE_KIND_VALIDATE.

